## Key Learnings

- XSS vulnerabilities occur when applications incorrectly handle untrusted user input.
- Reflected and Stored XSS differ mainly in how the malicious input is delivered and persisted.
- Proper input validation and output encoding are important defenses against XSS.
- Security controls such as Content Security Policy can provide an additional layer of protection.
- XSS testing should only be performed against authorized applications and controlled environments.

